class.description:
The preview of the Fornalha. [method load_asset] reads a [code].glb[/code] or [code].gltf[/code] file at runtime, with [GLTFDocument], so the asset needs no import. The asset stands on a floor at the center, and the camera frames the asset by its bounding box and turns around it slowly. The scene has a [DirectionalLight3D] with shadows and a procedural sky, and it follows the rendering settings of the project, including the [EretheaQuality] preset.
The asset can be replaced at any time with [method load_asset], without restarting. While [member auto_reload] is on, the preview also reloads the asset when its file changes on disk.
Without a project, the engine can start this scene by itself: [code]erethea --erethea-preview=asset.glb[/code]. With [code]--erethea-preview-capture=image.png[/code] it saves an image of the window after a few frames and exits, which is useful for tests. See "Prévia para a Fornalha" in [code]erethea/README.md[/code] for all the arguments and for how to embed the preview with LibGodot.
[codeblock]
var preview = EretheaPreview.new()
add_child(preview)
var error = preview.load_asset("C:/assets/dragon.glb")
if error != OK:
    push_error("The asset can't be shown.")
[/codeblock]
